-- Semasa · bring ws.regulab Studio's drafts, posts and ideas into Semasa (Wan, 27 Sep 2026: "go migrate").
-- PART 3 OF 3: the 66 posts Studio already published, kept as history
-- Run the three parts IN ORDER (1, 2, 3), each once, in the SQL editor, after 001–019. Each part is one transaction:
-- it goes in whole or not at all. Safe to run again: a row already brought over is skipped, never doubled.
--
-- SAFE IN A SHARED PROJECT (KPI): rows are ADDED to semasa_ideas and semasa_posts only. Nothing is changed or deleted,
-- no table, policy or function is touched, and no other app's data is read or written.
--
-- WHAT COMES OVER (Studio's store read 27 Sep 2026 08:53 UTC):
--   ideas: 118  (80 drafted, 37 rejected, 1 open -> 'error', so the bot does not write it by itself)
--   posts: 106  (36 drafts + 1 approved -> 'draft'; 3 scheduled -> 'scheduled'; 66 posted -> 'posted')
--
-- NOTHING HERE CAN POST. Semasa's publisher only sends a post approved INSIDE Semasa. Every imported post is a draft,
-- or 'scheduled'/'posted', which Semasa never sends. Studio's delivery records (Buffer / LinkedIn ids) are kept in
-- `published`, so even a live Semasa publisher skips every channel Studio already posted to.
-- Studio's 3 scheduled posts are still in Buffer and Studio still posts them: here they are locked and hold their slot.
-- Pictures do not come over (Studio's cards are not hosted where Semasa can read them), so a ws.regulab draft shows
-- "instagram needs an image" until a picture is made or attached. A carousel's words come over as its slides.
-- Until Studio is retired, approving the same story in BOTH systems posts it twice.
-- The Activity log gets ONE line for the whole import (written by part 3), not one per row.
begin;

-- the per-row log lines the inserts above just wrote (this transaction only): the import is one line, in part 3
